\section{Profile}
Systems engineer with over 25 years in Linux infrastructure, including 15
years writing production code.  Most recently worked as a Golang engineer on
Cloudflare's authoritative DNS routing team, after several years there as a
site reliability engineer.  Alongside this, maintains \textbf{util-linux},
the core utility suite included in all Linux distributions, with over 1,800
merged changes since 2010, and co-maintains \textbf{ping} as part of the
iputils project.  Holds a patent from Cloudflare for IP address decoupling
in distributed cloud networks.  Available immediately.

\section{Highlights}
\begin{itemize}
\itemsep 0em
\item Over \textbf{1,800 merged patches} to util-linux since 2010, and a
      fixed \href{https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/cve-2015-5218}{CVE} in
      that codebase.
\item Maintains \textbf{ping} for the iputils project, and is an official
      maintainer of \textbf{GNU Hello}.
\item Over \textbf{3,500 accepted open source contributions} across around
      40 projects since 2009.
\item Co-inventor, with Marwan Fayed and Pavel Odintsov, on a
      \textbf{Cloudflare patent} for decoupling IP address bindings in a
      distributed cloud network.
\item Built and ran a DNS platform serving over 20,000 domains at
      TeliaSonera, and worked on Cloudflare's authoritative DNS routing.
\item Wrote \href{https://dhcpd-pools.sourceforge.net/}{dhcpd-pools} from
      scratch and has maintained it since 2006, using autoconf, automake,
      static analysis tools, gdb, valgrind and perf.
\end{itemize}

