\section{Experience}

\textbf{Software Engineer, DNS Team (previously Site Reliability Engineer)} - Cloudflare \textit{Jul 2015 – Jul 2026}
\begin{itemize}
\itemsep 0em
\item Moved from site reliability engineering into a full-time Golang role
      on the authoritative DNS team, working on DNS routing across a network
      spanning tens of global co-locations.
\item As an SRE, covered on-call, attack mitigation and release engineering.
      Was asked to formalise the company's release process because of the
      volume of releases going through it.  Built monitoring around
      Prometheus and Grafana.
\item Co-invented a patented approach to decoupling IP address bindings from
      their use in a distributed cloud network.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Senior Systems Administrator / Infrastructure Architect} - lastminute.com \textit{Sep 2012 – Jun 2015}
\begin{itemize}
\itemsep 0em
\item Moved legacy infrastructure onto Puppet, Foreman and Pulp, and
      introduced Jenkins pipelines for developer self-service.
\item Wrote the technical plan for moving the company's data centre from the
      US to Europe, covering provisioning and configuration management,
      using GitLab and r10k.
\item Worked with distributed teams in London, India and Texas on
      monitoring, inventory, account management and orchestration, while
      maintaining PCI compliance.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Systems Engineer} - TomTom \textit{Sep 2008 – Aug 2012}
\begin{itemize}
\itemsep 0em
\item Owned production operations for \href{https://plan.tomtom.com/}{TomTom
      Route Planner}: change management, monitoring, security and
      performance, working closely with several developer teams.  In
      hindsight, this was DevOps before the term was in common use.
\item Led two data centre migrations, introduced Puppet configuration
      management, and rebuilt DNS management and server provisioning.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Principal Engineer (Consultant)} - Capgemini Finland \textit{Jan 2007 – Aug 2008}
\begin{itemize}
\itemsep 0em
\item Delivered order processing systems for a retail client handling billions
      of euros in annual order volume.
\item Designed an anycast DNS architecture for Nokia Siemens Networks, and
      supported enterprise Unix estates (AIX, HP-UX, Oracle RAC) for several
      clients.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{DNS Hostmaster Team Lead / Web Portal Administrator} - TeliaSonera \textit{Apr 2000 – Dec 2006}
\begin{itemize}
\itemsep 0em
\item Redesigned and ran a DNS platform serving over 20,000 domains at
      around 1GB per hour of recursive traffic, on Linux with F5 BIG-IP load
      balancing.
\item Modernised the company web portal, moving from Vignette V4 to V5,
      introducing Bluecoat reverse proxies and LDAP based authentication.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Earlier roles:} RTT Ohjelmistopankki \textit{1999–2000}, Novo Group \textit{1999}.

\section{Open Source}
\begin{itemize}
\itemsep 0em
\item \textbf{util-linux - maintainer, 2010 to present.}  Over 1,800 merged
